{
 "format": "damap",
 "version": 1,
 "id": "33",
 "name": "Riverhaven West Gate",
 "file": "Map33_Riverhaven_West_Gate.xml",
 "includes": [
  "Map33a_Road_to_Therenborough.xml"
 ],
 "rooms": [
  {"id":1,"x":100,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven, River Road West","descriptions":["The wooden palisade of the town wall runs down into the river, ending in the West Tower.  A narrow gate allows exit from the town into the countryside.  South of the road, a narrow strip of muddy ground surrounds numerous shanties where the local fishermen draw up their boats and work on their nets.  Small but well-kept houses line the northern side of the road where some of the more prosperous fisherfolk dwell."],"exits":[{"to":0,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":0,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":2,"exit":"go","move":"go gate"}],"aliases":["Riverhaven"],"linksTo":"Map30_Riverhaven.xml"},
  {"id":2,"x":40,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven Exterior, Southwest Gate","descriptions":["A narrow gate leads through the fortified wall here, providing travelers with access to the town.  Too small for wagons, this area's peacefulness is shattered only by the occasional hoof-beat.  Through the gate can be viewed a mixed selection of dwellings.  To the south a guard stands in a tower carefully watching the horizon, ready to sound the alarm if needed.  A wide, well traveled path heads off to the northwest."],"exits":[{"to":3,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":27,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":1,"exit":"go","move":"go gate"}]},
  {"id":3,"x":20,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven, Outside the Southwest Gate","descriptions":["The wooden parapets of the West Tower jut into the sky like bared teeth where the town wall sinks into the slow-flowing waters of the river.  A twisting path, almost completely overgrown with rambling blackberry bushes, leads westward from the foot of the guard tower and onward through the undergrowth toward the shore of Lake Gwenalion."],"exits":[{"to":2,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":4,"exit":"go","move":"go path"}]},
  {"id":4,"x":0,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven, Stony Path","descriptions":["The path stumbles over loose rocks and stones as it turns toward the south and pushes on through dense bracken and brambles.  Overhanging branches and thorny stems snatch at hair and clothing as travelers make their determined progress toward the lake, the vegetation whipping back to smother the path as soon as a body has passed through."],"exits":[{"to":5,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":3,"exit":"go","move":"go blackberry bushes"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":5,"x":0,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven, Stony Path","descriptions":["The seemingly thick undergrowth is sufficiently thin in spots to allow a tantalizing glimpse of glittering Lake Gwenalion, its waters shimmering silently between the branches of a lofty pine that blocks direct progress toward the shore.  The trail shifts unwillingly to the west, pushing its way through a thick clump of ferns and into a small clearing."],"exits":[{"to":4,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":6,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":6,"x":-20,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Pine Woods, Needlethatch Clearing","descriptions":["A spongy carpet of fallen pine needles greets the foot with a pleasant softness where the trail opens out in a circle of tall evergreens.  Several log cabins nestle amongst the trees, their squat chimneys draping the still air in a soft blue veil of pine-scented smoke.  The intermittent twitter of unseen birds drifts down from the branches overhead."],"exits":[{"to":5,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":7,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":7,"x":-40,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Pine Woods, Rocky Slope","descriptions":["The trail slips down a rocky slope, passing between clusters of cabins and shifting from side to side where mossy boulders prevent direct passage down toward the lakeshore.  Drifting up from the lakeshore, a cool breeze brings with it the smell of damp peat and the occasional faint splash of oars dipping deeply into still waters."],"exits":[{"to":6,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":8,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":8,"x":-40,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Pine Woods, Rocky Slope","descriptions":["Traces of sand mix with the damp earth as the path nears the shoreline and continues its gentle slope toward the water.  A low-growing tangle of ivy spills across the path from its bed at the front door of a cabin, giving off the sharp smell of crushed greenery where its leaves and stems have strayed too close to passing boots."],"exits":[{"to":7,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":9,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":9,"x":-40,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven, Gwenalion Shore","descriptions":["As if held back by some invisible hand, the thick growth of trees and bracken stops suddenly at the edge of the nearby woods, the path wresting itself free like an escaped convict from the confinement of the trees.  Spreading as far as the eye can see, the blue-green shoreline of Lake Gwenalion slips silently into the distance, vanishing eventually into the thin mist that cloaks the horizon in silvery grey."],"exits":[{"to":8,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":10,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":112,"exit":"go","move":"go leather tent"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":10,"x":-60,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven, Gwenalion Shore","descriptions":["A narrow path runs around the edge of the lake, in parts rocky and barren and elsewhere softly luxuriating in lush grasses and ferns.  Here, browned pine needles combine with sand and shingle around a tiny cove, where peaty waters lap the shore and envelope a huddle of fishermens' cottages in the gentle, sibilant lullaby of washing waves."],"exits":[{"to":9,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":11,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":11,"x":-80,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven, Gwenalion Shore","descriptions":["Following the soft curve of the shoreline, a small fleet of fishing boats rests on the shingle.  Coils of sodden greenish rope lash the boats to wooden posts dotting the rocky shore, alongside rows of mesh nets spread out to dry between excursions to the varied and profitable fishing in the center of the lake."],"exits":[{"to":10,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":12,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":12,"x":-100,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven, Gwenalion Shore","descriptions":["Looking out over the lake's sparkling expanse, a group of low stone cottages sits back from the path, the weathered grey of their thatched roofs blending into the misty woodland behind them.  Tiny waves lap the shore, the shallow waters at the edge of the lake quietly reporting the distant passage of barges between Riverhaven and Langenfirth."],"exits":[{"to":11,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":13,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":13,"x":-120,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Gwenalion Shore, Deep Gulch","descriptions":["The shoreline darts back toward the trees to form an angular cove surrounded by overhanging rocks.  Deep waters submerge the narrow chasm, swelling from their stillness only occasionally with the remote motion of a large vessel across the lake, and slapping softly against the roofs of the small caves on the waterline.  A few cottages amidst the trees enjoy this tranquil location."],"exits":[{"to":14,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":12,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":14,"x":-120,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Gwenalion Shore, Deep Gulch","descriptions":["The lakeside path narrows to a crooked trail as it picks its way gingerly around the rocky cove, further passage westward blocked by a precarious stony outcrop.  Low-lying crabgrass and clementines punctuate the path as it leads past some moss-grown cottages and turns back into the woods lining the lake.  To the southwest, the unclaimed wilds of the shoreline disappear around a sharp, unassailable promontory."],"exits":[{"to":15,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":13,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":15,"x":-120,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Pine Woods, Evergreen Path","descriptions":["The path slips back into the cool evergreen woods and twists toward a grassy clearing among the pines.  To the northwest, a rocky trail climbs a steep incline between wafting fiddlehead ferns, its covering of thick green moss damp and slippery underfoot.  A group of log cabins nestles in the fork between the paths, clinging determinedly to the uneven terrain."],"exits":[{"to":16,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":14,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":25,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rocky trail"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":16,"x":-100,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Pine Woods, Coldspring Clearing","descriptions":["A thick carpet of lush green grass spreads in a perfect circle formed by a group of stately pines.  A constant, cool breeze drifts between the cottages and cabins that occupy this idyllic spot, carrying with it the fragrance of the forest and the gentle melody of birdsong from the canopy of deep green branches overhead."],"exits":[{"to":17,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":15,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":23,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":17,"x":-80,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Pine Woods, Coldspring Clearing","descriptions":["A slight thinning of the trees and undergrowth allows for a glimpse of the lake to the southeast, its deep waters glinting silently below the wooded promontory.  Shards of shattered moonlight reflect faintly from the lake's surface and dance among the branches like mischievous sprites, soaking the area in a soft, silvery luminence.","A slight thinning of the trees and undergrowth allows for a glimpse of the lake to the southeast, its deep waters glinting silently below the wooded promontory.  Shards of shattered sunlight reflect faintly from the lake's surface and dance among the branches like mischievous sprites, bathing the area in a dappled golden glow."],"exits":[{"to":18,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":16,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":18,"x":-80,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Pine Woods, Coldspring Clearing","descriptions":["Gauzy curtains billow from the wide-open window of one cottage, their primary colors contrasting cheerfully with the muted greens and browns of this wooded clearing.  In the peaty, rich soil outside its front door, a collection of sun-bleached shells and pebbles forms an abstract design, their less-perfect neighbors lying scattered about the path."],"exits":[{"to":17,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":19,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":19,"x":-100,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Pine Woods, Coldspring Clearing","descriptions":["Several cottages and cabins surround a fire ring of smooth, blackened stones that lay beneath an ancient pine.  The tree's weighty boughs bend under the strain of their great age, reaching down to brush gently against even the lowest rooftop and sprinkling a fragrant shower of needles around the area with every whisper of wind."],"exits":[{"to":18,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":20,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":20,"x":-120,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Pine Woods, Coldspring Clearing","descriptions":["The murmur of gently lapping waves indicates this clearing is close to the shore of Lake Gwenalion, although the dense undergrowth of wild peppermint and silverleaf vine blocks any view of the water.  The soft, sleepless sound lulls the senses and wraps the homes here in a restful but unending music."],"exits":[{"to":19,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":21,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":24,"exit":"go","move":"go gap"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":21,"x":-140,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Pine Woods, Coldspring Clearing","descriptions":["The grassy turf underfoot is porous and loamy, supporting a lush growth of mossy thyme and enormous flat-topped toadstools that scatter the area like stepping stones in a still green pond.  Many of the homes here take advantage of the fertile soil and cultivate small, fragrant herb gardens bordered by rows of white-painted rocks underneath their kitchen windows."],"exits":[{"to":20,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":22,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":22,"x":-140,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Pine Woods, Coldspring Clearing","descriptions":["The comforting aroma of woodsmoke and hearty home cooking hangs in the air, emanating from the cozy homes which nestle between the trees.  At the edge of the clearing, the vigorous undergrowth of mixed vines and ivies conspires to reclaim their former territory, but the daily endeavors of local residents to nurture a compromise with the wildlife seem to enjoy some success."],"exits":[{"to":21,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":23,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":23,"x":-120,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Pine Woods, Coldspring Clearing","descriptions":["Bubbling up from beneath the turf, a crystal-clear spring drenches the surrounding grass in a glistening, ice-cold pool.  Many sets of footprints circle the spring, where locals come to catch the sparkling water for drinking and brewing before it disappears once more below the surface to follow its fated path down to the lake and beyond."],"exits":[{"to":16,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":22,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":24,"x":-140,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Pine Woods, Gwenalion Shore","descriptions":["A steep shingle slope tumbles down from the treeline, where exposed roots and tangled stems struggle to keep their owners from toppling onto the wooden huts that occupy this sliver of beach.  From the distance, faint sounds of battle occasionally drift along the water's edge from the western wilds outside Riverhaven, adding an edge of tension to the otherwise peaceful atmosphere."],"exits":[{"to":20,"exit":"go","move":"go gap"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":25,"x":-140,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Pine Woods, Evergreen Trail","descriptions":["Like a giant stairway clambering up the side of the hill, a collection of enormous, flat rocks protrudes from the loamy earth on either side of the trail.  Tiny wooden huts cling to each broad ledge, depending for their stability on the surrounding trees which shelter the frail constructions from the worst of the elements."],"exits":[{"to":26,"exit":"up","move":"up"},{"to":15,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rocky trail"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":26,"x":-140,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Pine Woods, Lake View","descriptions":["High above the sparkling waters of Lake Gwenalion, a vast slab of bare rock juts out beyond the treeline, providing a magnificent view of the wooded wilds between here and Therenborough.  In the far distance, the low buildings and dense forestation of Langenfirth crouch around the lake's northwestern shore.  A series of fat pine logs, stripped of their rough bark, provides a pleasant place to sit and enjoy the breathtaking vista."],"exits":[{"to":25,"exit":"down","move":"down"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":27,"x":20,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven Exterior, Trodden Path","descriptions":["Many feet and wagons have used this path as is evident by the hard packed soil beneath your feet.  Looking to the northwest you see a small building in the distance.  To the southeast lies the town, its high walls offering sanctuary to those who call it home.  Along the river bank to the south you watch as a trader works a mule that is pulling a small barge up stream."],"exits":[{"to":155,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":2,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":28,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":30,"exit":"go","move":"go winding path"}]},
  {"id":28,"x":-60,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven Exterior, Trodden Path","descriptions":["Before you stands the rustic stone building of the Barbarian Guild, badly in need of maintenance.  A simple arch provides entry without the assistance of a porch or walkway, the opening covered with a tattered and faded drape that acts as a makeshift door.  A small path heads off to the west around the guild."],"exits":[{"to":27,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":31,"exit":"go","move":"go overgrown trail"},{"to":91,"exit":"go","move":"go small path"},{"to":114,"exit":"go","move":"go faded drape"}]},
  {"id":30,"x":-120,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, Meadows","descriptions":["A feeling of openness pervades this plain of tall waving meadow grass.  A range of low rocky hills creates sharp-edged silhouettes on the horizon to the north. To the east at the end of a somewhat muddy looking trail is a small stand of trees circling a small inland pond.  Beyond the trees are the sturdy walls of Riverhaven."],"exits":[{"to":32,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":31,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":41,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":77,"exit":"go","move":"go muddy trail"},{"to":27,"exit":"go","move":"go winding path"}]},
  {"id":31,"x":-180,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, Meadows","descriptions":["Wildflowers, mingled with the waist-high grass, touch the surroundings with bright festive colors and a faint sweet fragrance that tickles the senses with each breeze rippling across the meadow.  A stone building lies at the end of an overgrown trail leading off to the south."],"exits":[{"to":41,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":30,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":39,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":28,"exit":"go","move":"go trail"}]},
  {"id":32,"x":-100,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, Meadow","descriptions":["The bleached half-buried skull of a large rat shows starkly against the dark soil of the meadow.  A patch of daisies grows around it as if planted in memoriam by a mourning rodent relative."],"exits":[{"to":33,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":30,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":41,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":34,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":33,"x":-80,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, Meadow","descriptions":["A lone waxy-leafed bush covered with bright pink blossoms pokes above the tall meadow grass.  Movement in the branches seems to indicate the presence of one or more small occupants.  Exposed bush roots extend through the grass and out over a bare spot of ground that slopes down to a rocky creek bank to the north."],"exits":[{"to":32,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":34,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":34,"x":-120,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, Meadow","descriptions":["The shadowed foothills to the north rise like brooding sentinels over the dark plains of meadow grass.  The chirrup of a cricket, or perhaps a small frog, rises from the surrounding vegetation, gentle accompaniment to the rustling of breeze-blown blades of grass.","The rocky foothills to the north rise like brooding sentinels over the sun-touched fields of meadow grass.  Clouds overhead cast fleeting shadows across the surrounding plain."],"exits":[{"to":33,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":32,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":41,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":35,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":35,"x":-160,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, Meadow","descriptions":["Vagrant breezes blowing across the lake to the west carry a cool touch of moisture that settles in a damp blanket across the meadow grass.  The sound of running water indicates the presence of a brook flowing to the north.","Vagrant breezes blowing across the lake to the west carry a cool touch of moisture that settles on the meadow grass in tiny glistening jewels.  A thin ribbon of blue cuts across the meadow to the north, indicating the presence of flowing water."],"exits":[{"to":34,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":41,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":36,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":36,"x":-200,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, Meadow","descriptions":["A huge, oddly shaped boulder blocks passage to the west.  The rough stone seems out of place, as if dropped by the hand of a giant on the outskirts of this flat plain."],"exits":[{"to":35,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":40,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":37,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":44,"exit":"go","move":"go gap"},{"to":90,"exit":"climb","move":"climb bank"},{"to":133,"exit":"climb","move":"climb huge boulder"}]},
  {"id":37,"x":-240,"y":-120,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, Lake Shore","descriptions":["Brightly-scaled fish leap among the waves of the lake like silver arrows shot into the sky.  Closer to the shoreline a family of geese paddles past in a lazy line, occasionally stopping to tip bottoms up in a hunt for sustenance below the surface of the water."],"exits":[{"to":42,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":36,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":38,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":132,"exit":"go","move":"go lake"}]},
  {"id":38,"x":-240,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, Lake Shore","descriptions":["Verdant grassland gives way to the loamy eastern shore of Lake Gwenalion.  A strip of shallow water laps at the narrow shore before diving into the restless depths of the lake bed.  Far to the west across the lake can be seen the vague outlines of buildings belonging to the community of Langenfirth."],"exits":[{"to":37,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":40,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":39,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":125,"exit":"go","move":"go lake"}]},
  {"id":39,"x":-200,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, Meadow","descriptions":["Intermittant rustlings provide evidence of small wild life residing in the tall meadow grass.  Further to the west spread the waters of Gwenalion Lake."],"exits":[{"to":40,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":31,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":38,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":40,"x":-200,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, Meadow","descriptions":["Trampled grass creates a criss-cross pattern of narrow trails across the lush meadow.  Here and there can be seen a bare spot of disturbed ground, small mounds of dirt piled next to narrow holes dug deep into the rich moist soil."],"exits":[{"to":36,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":41,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":39,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":38,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#C2B280","aliases":["RTT12","RT-HWG-HNG"]},
  {"id":41,"x":-140,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, Meadow","descriptions":["A delicate spider web woven amongst the dark green stalks of meadow grass glistens when brushed by a trembling breeze.  The ground here is pockmarked with several deep holes that appear to be the abodes of some sort of burrowing creature."],"exits":[{"to":34,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":32,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":30,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":31,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":40,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":35,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"aliases":["Shamans","Rams"]},
  {"id":42,"x":-240,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, Lake Shore","descriptions":["A huge boulder blocks passage to the north.  Along the lake front water washes in foamy ripples, dragging at dried grass and flower petals blown to the shore from the meadow to the east."],"exits":[{"to":37,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":43,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":133,"exit":"climb","move":"climb huge boulder"}]},
  {"id":43,"x":-260,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, Lake Shore","descriptions":["The spongy loam of the beach gives way to a sandy surface that is similar in color to the dark boulder blocking passage to the north and east.  Tiny fiddler crabs dash from the water lapping along the shore, then turn and scuttle back into the waves in an endless quest for food."],"exits":[{"to":42,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":130,"exit":"go","move":"go lake"},{"to":133,"exit":"climb","move":"climb huge boulder"}]},
  {"id":44,"x":-260,"y":-200,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Tunnels","descriptions":["A gap beneath a large boulder opens into a wide tunnel that curves in two directions around a submerged chunk of rock.  There is a distinct odor of rotting fish, mingled with the smell of rodent, pervading the tunnel.  It's not a particularly pleasant fragrance."],"exits":[{"to":48,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":45,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":47,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":36,"exit":"go","move":"go gap"}],"color":"#993300","aliases":["Mine"]},
  {"id":45,"x":-280,"y":-180,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, Tunnel","descriptions":["Scratch marks cover the walls of the tunnels, signature marks of creatures intent on expanding this underground haven."],"exits":[{"to":44,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":46,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":46,"x":-300,"y":-200,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, South Creek Bank","descriptions":["The floor of the tunnel seems to be composed of a mixture of sand, pebbles, crustacean shells and fish bones.  No doubt the carnivorous creatures living in the wilds have used the tunnels as a handy dining chamber for many years."],"exits":[{"to":47,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":45,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":47,"x":-280,"y":-220,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, South Creek Bank","descriptions":["Slow drips of water seep through the rock overhead and trail wet fingers down the sides of the tunnel before settling in muddy puddles on the moist and sandy floor."],"exits":[{"to":44,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":46,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":48,"x":-260,"y":-220,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Tunnels","descriptions":["A twisted tangle of roots seems to have blocked excavation further north, though fresh claw marks in the dirt between the roots indicate that burrowing efforts in that direction still continue."],"exits":[{"to":44,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":49,"exit":"go","move":"go roots"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":49,"x":-260,"y":-240,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["The passage here is very dark.  The only source of illumination seems to be the faint glow of the lichen growing on the walls.  The shadow of a twisted clump of roots further darkens the southern portion of the tunnel.","A twisted tangle of roots seems to block passage to the south, but through the roots can be seen the glow of a faint bit of light."],"exits":[{"to":50,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":48,"exit":"go","move":"go root"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":50,"x":-260,"y":-260,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["The glow of lichen growing along the walls of the tunnel provides the only source of illumination in this dark passage.","A dim, hazy light from the southern end of the tunnel casts a minimal amount of illumination over the surrounding area."],"exits":[{"to":51,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":49,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":51,"x":-260,"y":-280,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["Walls of rock imbedded in hard packed dirt begin to give way to passages burrowed out between solid chunks of stone.  Deep scratches mar the surface of many large boulders where animals have made a futile attempt to extend this underground burrow."],"exits":[{"to":52,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":50,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":52,"x":-260,"y":-300,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["Twisted tunnels bend off in several directions, some passages too narrow to allow anything bigger than a small rodent to squeeze through, others big enough to admit several people walking side by side."],"exits":[{"to":59,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":58,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":54,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":51,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":53,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":53,"x":-280,"y":-320,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["Several trickles of water collect in a small pool at the end of the passageway.  The water gleams faintly in the subdued glow of the lichen lining the damp walls.  Dark and oily, it looks as unsavory as it smells, but the multitude of animal tracks pressed into the muddy tunnel floor around the pool indicates that it is a popular source of water for the denizens of the tunnels."],"exits":[{"to":52,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":54,"x":-240,"y":-300,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["A crooked passage branches off here.  Small growths of fungus and lichen crowd the mud-covered walls."],"exits":[{"to":55,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":52,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":55,"x":-220,"y":-300,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["The dark sandstone rock crumbles into muddy earth.  Trickles of water slowly drip down tendrils of brown moss clinging to claw-like marks etched into the sides of the tunnel."],"exits":[{"to":56,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":54,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":56,"x":-200,"y":-320,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["A small niche lies to the north, a nook carved into the damp soil by thick claws.  Overhead tree roots, stripped bare of protective dirt, rot in the damp, fetid climate of the tunnels."],"exits":[{"to":55,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":57,"exit":"go","move":"go niche"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":57,"x":-180,"y":-320,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["This small cramped area appears to have once been the nest of some creature with very unsanitary housekeeping habits.  It's dark, it's damp, and it's smelly, and there is about the place a feeling of darkness that extends beyond the mere fact that there is little light here.  The glowing lichen on the walls grows in unusual, almost runic patterns."],"exits":[{"to":56,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":58,"x":-240,"y":-320,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["A steady whisper like the muffled sound of running water can be heard in this area of the tunnel.  Damp lines of moisture trickle down the walls on every side."],"exits":[{"to":52,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":59,"x":-260,"y":-320,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["The tunnel here is dark with illuminating patches of lichen growing very sparsely on walls composed almost entirely of solid rock.  The rough texture of natural stone along each side of the tunnel has been marred with angular planes of what seems to be deliberately chiseled rock."],"exits":[{"to":52,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":60,"x":-260,"y":-340,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["The tunnel seems to go on forever, too narrow to turn around.  All you can do is keep crawling and hope to reach the end soon."],"exits":[{"to":59,"exit":"none","move":"none"},{"to":61,"exit":"none","move":"none"}],"aliases":["Dusk Ogres"]},
  {"id":61,"x":-260,"y":-360,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["Water trickles down the lichen that line the rocky walls, collecting in dimly glowing puddles along the sides of the tunnel.  The light is faint and casts eerie shadows that seem to move along the limits of your vision.  A pile of rubble surrounds the base of a passage leading upward to the south, evidently detritus from a cleared rockslide."],"exits":[{"to":62,"exit":"north","move":"north"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":62,"x":-260,"y":-380,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["The passage slopes down to the north, twisting as it works around a rough-carved granite pillar that glistens in the dim light.  Rivulets of water seep through the ceiling to run down the walls, glowing from the minerals and lichen.  A few of the cracks in the tunnel's roof are wide enough to allow a thin trickle to fall from ceiling to floor, quickly rolling down the passage into the darkness below."],"exits":[{"to":61,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":66,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":63,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":63,"x":-280,"y":-400,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["Water gathers in numerous pools at the low point of the passage, the deepest no more than knee-high for a Halfling.  Twisted taproots work their way through the rock, descending like close-packed pillars as they seek out the moisture necessary for their survival.  The thick roots are coated with a sticky sap that makes travel difficult, catching at arms and legs that brush against them."],"exits":[{"to":65,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":62,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":64,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":64,"x":-300,"y":-420,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["The path through the caverns bends sharply as it picks its way through tangles of sticky roots.  Patches of lichen cling to the walls giving off a pallid phosphorescent glow that casts more shadows than illumination."],"exits":[{"to":65,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":63,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":65,"x":-280,"y":-440,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["Passages branch off in all directions, threading their ways through the maze of interwoven roots.  Glowing red eyes peer through the tangle, following your movements, but skittering back into the shadows whenever you draw too close."],"exits":[{"to":69,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":68,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":63,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":64,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":66,"x":-260,"y":-400,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["A dull roar of swift-flowing water fills the tunnel, far too much to be accounted for by the shallow pools lining the walls.  Close-spaced pillars run from floor to ceiling leaving just enough room to pick a path between them."],"exits":[{"to":67,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":70,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":62,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":67,"x":-240,"y":-420,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["Sticky tendrils as thick as an Elf's arm shoot off in all directions from the pillar-like taproots that block the tunnel, grasping impartially at whatever skin or clothing may brush against them.  The splash of footsteps through puddles of water echoes about the cavern."],"exits":[{"to":70,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":66,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":68,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":68,"x":-260,"y":-440,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["The pools that dot the cavern's floor become shallower to the north, and the tangled roots are less of an obstruction, though still dense enough to entrap the unwary.  A faint breeze carries with it the scent of fresh grass to alleviate some of the musty stench that marks the deeper areas."],"exits":[{"to":69,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":67,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":65,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":69,"x":-260,"y":-460,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["The breeze flows down the tunnel, mingling the scent of cropped grass with the dank smell of packed earth.  No light from the surface penetrates the darkness of the tunnels.  Pallid lichens line the walls and cast a faint glow that make beads of sap glisten upon the columnar taproots."],"exits":[{"to":68,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":65,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":72,"exit":"up","move":"up"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":70,"x":-220,"y":-400,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["Rope-thick rootlets branch off from massive taproots to form tangled snarls that glisten with sticky sap.  The air is redolent with the dank, musty smell of stagnant water and too little ventilation, and a darker scent of rotting meat.  From time to time, scuffling footsteps can be heard in the passage, and shadows move at the edge of your vision."],"exits":[{"to":71,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":66,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":67,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":71,"x":-240,"y":-380,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["Phosphorescent fungi cast a faint glow, just enough to reveal a shifting flock of bats nesting along the cavern's ceiling.  From time to time, one of the creatures flexes its wings with a dry rustle before settling back to its sleep.  Other, less easily identifiable shadows move just out of the range of your vision, accompanied by a dry coughing noise or the scraping of nails against the floor."],"exits":[{"to":70,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":72,"x":-180,"y":-380,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["Tendrils of mist twist along the floor, hazily illuminated by clumps of phosphorescent lichen that cling to the slick surface.  Sandstone walls, dark along the bottom and lighter at the top, give mute testimony to the peril of water in the tunnels.  Although the floor is dry enough now, the waist-high border between dark and light is evidence of past floods inundating the caverns and all within."],"exits":[{"to":73,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":69,"exit":"down","move":"down"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":73,"x":-160,"y":-400,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Dark Tunnels","descriptions":["Light creeps in from the surface to bathe the cavern in a diffuse glow.  Detritus blown by wind and rain collects along the corners, a moldering pile of compost from which spindly weeds cling tenaciously to life, stretching upwards in search of the illumination they require.  No amount of determination can make up for the lack, though, and the plant life will soon die, its remains adding to the rotting mess along the floor until some other sprouts to repeat the cycle of life and decay."],"exits":[{"to":72,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":74,"exit":"up","move":"up"}],"color":"#993300"},
  {"id":74,"x":-140,"y":-400,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, North Meadow","descriptions":["Dried blossoms blown in by the wind decorate the base of a large rough boulder to the west.  The boulder joins to rock of the same composition that rises from the loamy soil of the meadow and spreads out in a long curving line of foothills.  A steeply banked creek cuts across the meadow to the south."],"exits":[{"to":76,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":75,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":73,"exit":"go","move":"go gap"},{"to":86,"exit":"climb","move":"climb bank"}],"aliases":["Young Ogres"]},
  {"id":75,"x":-100,"y":-400,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, North Meadow","descriptions":["Singular trees dot the meadow as it climbs its way toward a dense forest to the north.  The sound of running water rises from a steep creek bank to the south."],"exits":[{"to":96,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":95,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":74,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":76,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":85,"exit":"climb","move":"climb bank"}]},
  {"id":76,"x":-120,"y":-440,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, North Meadow","descriptions":["A high ridge of rocky foothills rises in a nearly perpendicular angle to the west, the summit of the hills far out of reach overhead. The ground of the meadow here is soft with a thick layer of crumpled leaves that have drifted in from the dense stands of deciduous trees growing to the north."],"exits":[{"to":96,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":75,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":74,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":77,"x":-60,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Sylvan Pond, Mud Flats","descriptions":["Higher ground combined with runoff from the pond has created a muddy swamp.  Puddles of water intersperse with rivulets that travel to a deep depression beneath a hollow log."],"exits":[{"to":78,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":30,"exit":"go","move":"go muddy trail"}]},
  {"id":78,"x":-40,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Sylvan Pond, Mud Flats","descriptions":["The water of the pond seems to have backed up over land that was once dry.  Several toppled tree trunks are all that remain of the willows that grew here."],"exits":[{"to":79,"exit":"north","move":"swim north"},{"to":77,"exit":"southwest","move":"swim southwest"},{"to":89,"exit":"northwest","move":"swim northwest"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":79,"x":-40,"y":-180,"z":0,"title":"Sylvan Glade, Pond","descriptions":["Shaded by the branches of the willow trees, the pond water is comfortably cool and clean.  The bank of the pond slopes down from the east while the pond itself extends further out in several directions."],"exits":[{"to":80,"exit":"north","move":"swim north"},{"to":78,"exit":"south","move":"swim south"},{"to":89,"exit":"west","move":"swim west"},{"to":134,"exit":"go","move":"go pond bank"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":80,"x":-40,"y":-200,"z":0,"title":"Sylvan Glade, Lily Pads","descriptions":["Out of the shade of the trees to the east the water sparkles in the warming light of the sun.  Several large and surprisingly sturdy-looking lily pads float on the surface of the pond.","Free from the shadows of the trees to the east, the water sparkles in the light of the Elanthian stars.  Several large and surprisingly sturdy-looking lily pads float on the surface of the pond."],"exits":[{"to":79,"exit":"south","move":"swim south"},{"to":89,"exit":"southwest","move":"swim southwest"},{"to":81,"exit":"northwest","move":"swim northwest"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":81,"x":-60,"y":-220,"z":0,"title":"Sylvan Glade, Creek Inlet","descriptions":["Fresh from its rapid passage over cleansing rocks and sand, the water of the pond is crystal clear and the silver flash of slender fish can be seen gliding along the smoothly pebbled bottom of the pond.","Water from a deep creek rushes into a small inland pond. Fresh from its passage over cleansing rocks and sand, the water is crystal clear and the shadowed forms of fish can be seen gliding through the darkened depths of the pond."],"exits":[{"to":80,"exit":"southeast","move":"swim southeast"},{"to":87,"exit":"west","move":"swim west"},{"to":82,"exit":"northwest","move":"swim northwest"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":82,"x":-80,"y":-240,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, North Creek Bank","descriptions":["The creek bed dead ends here with the rise of a perpendicular cliff to the east.  Water slaps against the face of the dark stone in a tumbling crashing spray, then swirls to the southeast where it empties into an open pond."],"exits":[{"to":81,"exit":"southeast","move":"swim southeast"},{"to":83,"exit":"northwest","move":"swim northwest"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":83,"x":-100,"y":-260,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, North Creek Bank","descriptions":["Rapidly-running water obscures the view of the creek bed, but dark shapes indicate the presence of rocks fairly close to the surface of the creek.  The banks of the creek are particularly slippery at this point, with no good hand or footholds available for climbing."],"exits":[{"to":82,"exit":"southeast","move":"swim southeast"},{"to":84,"exit":"west","move":"swim west"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":84,"x":-120,"y":-260,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, North Creek Bank","descriptions":["Movement other than the flow of the current can be seen beneath the somewhat turbulent water of the creek.  Silver-scaled fish, scuttling water beetles and colorful shellfish seem to exist in abundance all around you."],"exits":[{"to":83,"exit":"east","move":"swim east"},{"to":85,"exit":"northwest","move":"swim northwest"},{"to":95,"exit":"climb","move":"climb bank"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":85,"x":-140,"y":-280,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, North Creek Bank","descriptions":["Wet, algae-coated rocks rise at nearly perpendicular angles along both sides of the creek.  Near the center of the creek an occasional twig or leaf floats by, bobbing like a storm-tossed ship before being sucked down by a sudden whirlpool breaking the surface of the flow."],"exits":[{"to":84,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":86,"exit":"west","move":"swim west"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":86,"x":-160,"y":-280,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, North Creek Bank","descriptions":["Water rushes swiftly over the rocky creek bed, dashing into submerged obstacles with liberal sprays of foam and white topped waves."],"exits":[{"to":85,"exit":"east","move":"swim east"},{"to":74,"exit":"climb","move":"climb bank"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":87,"x":-80,"y":-220,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, South Creek Bank","descriptions":["To the east, the creek widens into a small, placid inland pond surrounded by a stand of delicately drooping willow trees. The stony bank of the creek rises to the south."],"exits":[{"to":81,"exit":"east","move":"swim east"},{"to":88,"exit":"northwest","move":"swim northwest"},{"to":33,"exit":"climb","move":"climb bank"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":88,"x":-100,"y":-240,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, South Creek Bank","descriptions":["Algae-coated stones provide dry but slippery footing along the southern edge of the creek.  The shadowy forms of larger boulders can be seen beneath the water closer to the center of the creek."],"exits":[{"to":87,"exit":"southeast","move":"swim southeast"},{"to":94,"exit":"west","move":"swim west"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":89,"x":-60,"y":-180,"z":0,"title":"Sylvan Glade, Dam","descriptions":["A jumbled pile of logs, brush and other forest debris forms a natural dam at the western end of the pond.  Extending out from the tangle is a half submerged willow tree trunk."],"exits":[{"to":80,"exit":"northeast","move":"swim northeast"},{"to":79,"exit":"east","move":"swim east"},{"to":78,"exit":"southeast","move":"swim southeast"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":90,"x":-200,"y":-260,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, South Creek Bank","descriptions":["Water pours through a stony gap to the west, falling over a ragged-edged cliff in a crashing spray of white froth that pushes everything in its path down to the bottom of the creek bed. "],"exits":[{"to":93,"exit":"east","move":"swim east"},{"to":36,"exit":"climb","move":"climb bank"},{"to":135,"exit":"climb","move":"climb steep cliff"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":91,"x":-60,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Barbarian Guild, Training Yard","descriptions":["Wooden weapons of all kinds lie stacked about, no doubt the tools of training the next great warrior.  In the center of the yard, a senior guild member instructs a confused student on the finer art of pole arm fighting.  A simple split-rail fence defines this area and provides a perch for two young children who giggle and watch as they dream of the day they will train here.  A large, pedaled sharpening stone and a target dummy catch your eye."],"exits":[{"to":28,"exit":"go","move":"go small path"},{"to":92,"exit":"go","move":"go iron grate"},{"to":113,"exit":"go","move":"go wooden shack"}],"color":"#FFFF00","aliases":["Stamina"]},
  {"id":92,"x":-60,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Barbarian Guild, Lower Amphitheatre","descriptions":["Aromatic wooden planks are tightly joined to contain the tons of sod which comprise the walls of this pit.  Dug beneath the foundation of the Barbarians' Guild, it is cool and moist, perfectly suited to focused training.  Several painted panels adorn the walls, depicting warriors in various types of armor, executing different combat maneuvers."],"exits":[{"to":91,"exit":"climb","move":"climb wooden ladder"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Calenra"]},
  {"id":93,"x":-180,"y":-260,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, South Creek Bank","descriptions":["Algae-coated stones provide dry but slippery footing along the southern edge of the creek.  The shadowy forms of larger boulders can be seen beneath the water closer to the center of the creek.","Water runs past you, clear and fast, with occasional white-capped waves brushing over submerged stones.  There's no good place to ford the creek at this point, but it would be possible to swim along the shallower edges near the bank."],"exits":[{"to":90,"exit":"west","move":"swim west"},{"to":94,"exit":"southeast","move":"swim southeast"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":94,"x":-160,"y":-240,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, South Creek Bank","descriptions":["To the east, the creek widens into a small, placid inland pond surrounded by a stand of delicately drooping willow trees. The stony bank of the creek rises to the south.","A series of rocks, trapping deposits of silt and sand, has built a shallow ridge on the edge of the water, allowing for easy wading along this section of the creek.  The banks of the creek are steep and slippery, a definite hazard for climbers."],"exits":[{"to":93,"exit":"northwest","move":"swim northwest"},{"to":88,"exit":"east","move":"swim east"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":95,"x":-80,"y":-400,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, North Meadow","descriptions":["A lone oak balances precariously on the edge of the creek bank, exposed roots clinging desperately to the surrounding rock and soil.  Sun-starved meadow grass grows beneath the tree in sporadic patches, competing without much success with a carpet of moss that spreads around the base of the tree in lush profusion."],"exits":[{"to":97,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":99,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":75,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":96,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":96,"x":-80,"y":-440,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, North Meadow","descriptions":["Thickly interwoven branches of oak and maple block the sunlight in this southern portion of the woods.  Faint trails seem to cut through the heavy undergrowth of vines and brambles at the foot of the trees, but most appear to dwindle away to nonexistence after a few feet of travel.","Thickly interwoven branches of oak and maple cast deep night shadows in this southern portion of the woods. Faint trails seem to cut through the heavy undergrowth of vines and brambles at the foot of the trees, but most appear to dwindle away to nonexistence after a few feet of travel."],"exits":[{"to":97,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":99,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":95,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":76,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":97,"x":-60,"y":-440,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, North Meadow","descriptions":["A circle of stones surrounds a small firepit near a low outcropping of rocks.  Apparently some weary traveler paused here for a moment of rest."],"exits":[{"to":98,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":95,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":75,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":96,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":98,"x":-40,"y":-440,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, North Meadow","descriptions":["The underbrush is quite thick here near the forest edge.   Speckled motes of sunlight dance down through the leafy boughs above, picking out a small path that maneuvers its way around the trunks of the trees like a dusty serpent slithering through a maze.","The underbrush is quite thick here near the forest edge.  Dim starlight filters down through the leafy boughs above, picking out a small shadowed path that maneuvers its way around the trunks of the trees like a dusty serpent slithering through a maze."],"exits":[{"to":75,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":99,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":97,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":103,"exit":"go","move":"go path"}]},
  {"id":99,"x":-40,"y":-400,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, North Meadow","descriptions":["A line of ants trudges across a beaten section of grass toward a large ant hill, carrying the fruits of their labor down deep into the loamy meadow soil.  Hoofed footprints scattered across the ground look like they might belong to some species of goat or sheep.","The light of the stars picks out the tracks of some hoofed animal impressed in the rich meadow soil.  A whispering breeze blows the scent of wildflowers through the night air."],"exits":[{"to":98,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":100,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":95,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":97,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":100,"x":-20,"y":-400,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, North Meadow","descriptions":["A large flat rock rises from the soil here, somewhat rectangular in shape and smooth on the top.  Loose soil piled around the base suggests that one or more burrowing creatures has made themselves a cozy home beneath the stony shelter."],"exits":[{"to":102,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":101,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":99,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":98,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":101,"x":0,"y":-400,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, North Meadow","descriptions":["Forest encroaches onto meadow with the stark abruptness of an invading army.  Fallen leaves and wide spreading branches block all sun from the last of the meadow grass that struggles to grow in the crowded tangle of bramble bushes and tree trunks.  A small beaten animal track winds its way through the woods to the east."],"exits":[{"to":100,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":136,"exit":"go","move":"go winding track"}]},
  {"id":102,"x":0,"y":-420,"z":0,"title":"Wildland, NorthWest Forest","descriptions":["A dense growth of high thorny bushes chokes even the roots of the sturdy young oak trees struggling to grow in this spot.  Travel in any direction except back to the open meadow will be difficult if not impossible."],"exits":[{"to":100,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":103,"x":40,"y":-480,"z":0,"title":"Wildland, NorthWest Forest","descriptions":["A toppled oak has opened a window to the sky.  Hazy streams of light cut down through the pervading gloom of the woods to settle on an opportunistic patch of Oralana blossoms that show with a startling yellow brightness against the deep green moss creeping over the rotted wood of the oak.","A toppled oak has opened a window to the sky, giving a clear view of the stars.  Oralana blossoms clumped around the rotting oak touch the night air with their sweet perfume."],"exits":[{"to":104,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":105,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":107,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":98,"exit":"go","move":"go small path"}],"aliases":["Arbelogs"]},
  {"id":104,"x":60,"y":-480,"z":0,"title":"Wildland, NorthWest Forest","descriptions":["A land sink forms an irregular oval depression in this part of the woods, trapping rainfall and providing the ideal growth conditions for an extensive grove of aspen trees."],"exits":[{"to":103,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":105,"x":20,"y":-480,"z":0,"title":"Wildland, NorthWest Forest","descriptions":["The twitter of birds going about their daily business fills the surrounding woods.  Speckled beams of sunlight dance past the branches overhead and touch the blossoms and herbs growing on the forest floor like a bright benediction.","The soft coo of birds comfortably nested in the branches overhead pervade the night.  Somewhere not far distant, a chorus of crickets chirp, harmonious accompaniment to the rustle of leaves blown by a sighing wind."],"exits":[{"to":103,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":106,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":106,"x":0,"y":-480,"z":0,"title":"Wildland, NorthWest Forest","descriptions":["A dense growth of shrubs forms a cozy thicket snuggled up to a concave bend in the rocky ridge of foothills. Scuffed dirt and disturbed drifts of leaves suggest that some wild creature has chosen the thicket as its home."],"exits":[{"to":105,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":107,"x":20,"y":-500,"z":0,"title":"Wildland, NorthWest Forest","descriptions":["The trees here are old, their bark deeply fissured and covered with faded moss that trails from the trunks of the trees like a beard on the face of an ancient dwarf.  One majestic oak towers above the rest, branches spread wide like the arms of a king raised in royal benediction over the heads of his loyal retainers."],"exits":[{"to":103,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":108,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":138,"exit":"none","move":"ru boak;go fog"}]},
  {"id":108,"x":0,"y":-500,"z":0,"title":"Wildland, NorthWest Forest","descriptions":["The ground shifts from gently sloping woods to a jagged and quickly rising hill.  The increasing elevation discourages the growth of deciduous trees and woods give way to pine forest further up the hillside."],"exits":[{"to":107,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":109,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":109,"x":-20,"y":-500,"z":0,"title":"Wildland, NorthWest Forest","descriptions":["Clumps of pines obscure the view of the hill above and woods below, but a heavily-trodden path continues to curl lazily onward through the sweetly scented forest."],"exits":[{"to":110,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":108,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":110,"x":0,"y":-520,"z":0,"title":"Wildland, NorthWest Forest","descriptions":["Nooks and crannies filled with dirt by the wind and warmed by the sun provide a haven for clumps of glaysker blossoms.  Decorating the southern facing slopes of the foothills in deep hues of purple, they fill the air with their sweet, subtle scent."],"exits":[{"to":111,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":109,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":111,"x":20,"y":-520,"z":0,"title":"Wildland, NorthWest Forest","descriptions":["Dark and steep, an elevated cliff guards the way north, its face flat and rough in monolithic challenge.  High overhead a stunted pine grows, seemingly out of solid rock.  Balanced on a tiny outcropping, it clings with the tenacity of a Maiden's Tress vine to its chosen niche, roots seeking purchase in every tiny crack and cranny to be found in the unyielding stone."],"exits":[{"to":110,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":112,"x":-40,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Fallen Treasures","descriptions":["A soft carpet of green pine needles covers the floor of this spacious tent, muffling all sound and lending the air a light, refreshing scent.  Various pieces of furniture, all crafted from items scavenged in the forest, sit displayed for sale along the walls."],"exits":[{"to":9,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Windfeather","Fallen Treasures"]},
  {"id":113,"x":-80,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Grinta's Forge, Shop","descriptions":["A blast of hellish heat greets every visitor who enters the simple wooden shack, and a thin layer of greyish soot covers every surface.  The air hangs heavy with the acrid scent of melting steel.  A sweating Dwarven attendant leans against the far wall, next to a heavy leather flap through which you can hear a muffled pounding noise."],"exits":[{"to":91,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000"},
  {"id":114,"x":-50,"y":-50,"z":0,"title":"Barbarian Guild, Interior","descriptions":["Puddles merge across the floor where rainwater seeps from a sodden thatched roof, leaking winter after winter despite the guild's half-hearted efforts at a permanent lodging.  The summer months offer little respite from the moisture, trapped inside by walls of river rock and denied the sun's drying heat.  Still, the Barbarians here could care less, lounging about on wooden benches with all the pomp of noble knights in a king's court."],"exits":[{"to":28,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":115,"exit":"go","move":"go stone arch"}],"color":"#FF8000","aliases":["Barbarian Guild","Mo","GL Barbarian","RS Barbarian"]},
  {"id":115,"x":-40,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Barbarian Guild, Dormitory","descriptions":["A broad, guttered aisle runs down the center of this windowless outbuilding, a few flickering torches punctuating its plain walls.  Long shadows shudder in a chilly draft which persists regardless of the season and in spite of wads of straw packed into every crack in the masonry.  Rough woolen curtains hang loosely from metal hooks above numerous half-doors ranged evenly along either side of the passageway, twitching sullenly in the unwelcome breeze."],"exits":[{"to":116,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":114,"exit":"go","move":"go stone arch"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":116,"x":-30,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Barbarian Guild, Dormitory","descriptions":["Massive oak beams support the weathered roof, creaking and groaning with each bluster of breeze under the eaves.  Every slight sound echoes boldly around the building, reaching up into the rafters and rattling around the vaulted ceiling in search of escape.  Occasional shouts and laughter ring out from further down the hall and beyond, the occupants of this abode seeming quite unconcerned by the austerity of their accommodations."],"exits":[{"to":117,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":115,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":117,"x":-20,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Barbarian Guild, Dormitory","descriptions":["The vast slabs of river rock which form the walls and floor of the corridor clamp a cold dampness into the air.  Somewhere nearby, an invisible trickle of water drips slowly but steadily onto the ancient stone, its rhythm almost melodious in the resonant gloom.  Stacked raggedly against one wall, a tottering heap of worn-out armor items and old saddlery gives off the cloying odor of moist, moldy leather."],"exits":[{"to":118,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":116,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":118,"x":-10,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Barbarian Guild, Dormitory","descriptions":["A crude blackwood table squats beneath one of the hallway's infrequent torches, wedges of tightly-folded brownish paper propping up three of its misshapen legs.  Several rusted iron hayracks remain attached to the opposite wall, adequately serving their new purpose as holders for unfinished weapon parts and damaged armor that someone will eventually get around to fixing.  Outside one stall, a leaky water pump stands crookedly in a twisted iron bracket, dripping determinedly."],"exits":[{"to":119,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":117,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":119,"x":0,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Barbarian Guild, Dormitory","descriptions":["The passageway widens slightly as it turns a corner and proceeds northward toward a source of thin grey light.  Rather than lending any comfort, the comparative brightness only serves to emphasize the dormitory's stark functionality and its notable lack of homely cheer.  A few rickety wooden chairs and a couple of iron benches loiter in the corner of the hallway, providing an artless but relatively agreeable gathering-place for residents to sit and share tall tales from the battlefield."],"exits":[{"to":120,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":118,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":120,"x":0,"y":-70,"z":0,"title":"Barbarian Guild, Dormitory","descriptions":["This area boasts the outbuilding's solitary window.  Cracked and grimy and long sealed shut by years of damp and dust, only a small patch in the center of the aged pane has been rubbed almost free of dirt where many noses have pressed up against it.  Even direct sunlight in high summer can force only feeble, pallid rays to penetrate the gloom -- but no matter, since the decor hardly warrants closer inspection."],"exits":[{"to":121,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":119,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":121,"x":0,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Barbarian Guild, Dormitory","descriptions":["A ragged hole in the wall at shoulder level to a Gor'Tog serves no apparent purpose, and judging by its lack of form was originally inflicted by an irate individual with a large, blunt object.  Shards of displaced masonry lie scattered about the floor."],"exits":[{"to":122,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":120,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":122,"x":0,"y":-90,"z":0,"title":"Barbarian Guild, Dormitory","descriptions":["Lying askew across the flagstones, a faded tapestry rug forlornly attempts to bring a sense of homeliness to the otherwise spartan lodgings.  The struggling flame of a solitary torch throws lurching shadows from a vast dust-laden cobweb which stretches from one side of the lofty ceiling to the other, giving the unnerving impression that this dormitory is also home to an enormous eight-legged inmate."],"exits":[{"to":123,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":121,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":123,"x":0,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Barbarian Guild, Dormitory","descriptions":["An unruly pile of greying straw bales sprawls across the passageway here, requiring passers-by to turn sideways and press up against the wall in order to squeeze past.  Clouds of dust and spores billow from the ancient bedding with every whisper of draft, scattering in the cold air before settling in a thick, musty layer over everyone and everything in the vicinity.  Muffled squeaks and scuffles can be heard from deep within the pile."],"exits":[{"to":124,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":122,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":124,"x":0,"y":-110,"z":0,"title":"Barbarian Guild, Dormitory","descriptions":["Closing off the end of the outbuilding, an enormous double door hangs heavily on rusted iron hinges so solidly sealed it would take a blacksmith to get them open.  Great drafty gaps surround the towering oaken slabs, allowing a persistent breeze to penetrate the building and bring with it the faint smell of peaty lake water and trodden grass.  From a distance floats the remote cry of the hunter and the hunted, their voices intermingled and indistinguishable."],"exits":[{"to":123,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":125,"x":-280,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Gwenalion Lake, East","descriptions":["Though tinted a light brown by decaying forest matter, the water of the lake retains its translucent qualities.  Small snails crawl over the algae-coated rocks lining the bottom of the lake and fingerling fish dart amongst a thick stand of cattails growing near the edge of the bank."],"exits":[{"to":132,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":126,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":127,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":38,"exit":"go","move":"go shore"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":126,"x":-300,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Gwenalion Lake, East","descriptions":["An occasional plop and rippled splash disturbing the surface of the lake provides a quiet counterpoint to the soft lapping sound of waves against the eastern shore."],"exits":[{"to":127,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":132,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":125,"exit":"east","move":"east"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":127,"x":-300,"y":-120,"z":0,"title":"Gwenalion Lake, East","descriptions":["Rising swells carry small bits of flotsam along the surface of the lake.  Deeper in the water a moderately strong undertow flows in a northeastern direction, swaying stalks of tall lake grass like trees in a wind."],"exits":[{"to":128,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":131,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":132,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":125,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":126,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":128,"x":-300,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Gwenalion Lake, East","descriptions":["Staying afloat proves to be a test of skill as the lake bed plummets to indiscernible depths.  Wind blown waves lick at the tip of a rock poking out of the water, just out of reach to the west.  A tickling swirl of water indicates the the presence of fish passing through the murky depths below."],"exits":[{"to":129,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":130,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":131,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":132,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":127,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":129,"x":-300,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Gwenalion Lake, East","descriptions":["The water here is very deep, and hard undertows pull relentlessly at your body, dragging you below the waves with monotonous regularity.  Occasional whirlpools spring up around you, increasing the danger of remaining this far into the lake for any great length of time."],"exits":[{"to":130,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":131,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":128,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":130,"x":-280,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Gwenalion Lake, East","descriptions":["A large dark rock sprawls across the beach and into the water like an enormous beached whale, blocking all passage to the east and north.  Shattered shells of mollusks and crayfish litter the nooks and crannies up the sides of the rock, bleached white by the sun and gleaming against the darker background of the stone."],"exits":[{"to":131,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":128,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":129,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":43,"exit":"go","move":"go shore"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":131,"x":-280,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Gwenalion Lake, East","descriptions":["The lake bottom dips drastically at this point and darker, deeper water spreads to the north and west.  Leafy tops of water plants growing in the lake reach toward the surface, roots and stalks lost from sight in the depths below."],"exits":[{"to":130,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":132,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":127,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":128,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":129,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":132,"x":-280,"y":-120,"z":0,"title":"Gwenalion Lake, East","descriptions":["Further out on the unsettled waters of the lake are the shadowy shapes of fishing boats bobbing and rocking like oversized cradles riding on the wind-tossed waves.  A vocal frog closer to shore chirrups his loneliness to the night sky, providing regular counterpoint to the sound of water lapping against the loamy beach."],"exits":[{"to":131,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":125,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":126,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":127,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":128,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":37,"exit":"go","move":"go shore"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":133,"x":-240,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven West Wilds, Boulder Top","descriptions":["A strong breeze blows across the top of the boulder, carrying the sharp scent of lake water mingled with the fainter fragrance of meadow grass."],"exits":[{"to":36,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":134,"x":-20,"y":-180,"z":0,"title":"Sylvan Glade, Pond Shore","descriptions":["The rhythmic chirp of frogs provides a gentle background music to the sylvan setting of a deep clear pond.  Weeping willows trail delicate branches in the water, trembling the smooth surface with each passing breeze.  A leaf-strewn bank slopes gently down to the water."],"exits":[{"to":79,"exit":"go","move":"go pond bank"}]},
  {"id":135,"x":-220,"y":-260,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Overlook","descriptions":["Graffiti covers the face of the cliff, presumably left by local youths attempting to impress a loved one with their daring.  Mist-soaked rock makes the cliff a treacherous climb going up, and even more so on the way down, but time and weather has provided a risky-looking alternate route.  A water-filled stone chute winds its way down from the cliff-top, twisting in and out of the waterfall on its way, before emptying into the creek far, far below."],"exits":[{"to":90,"exit":"climb","move":"climb steep cliff"}]},
  {"id":136,"x":20,"y":-400,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven Wilds, Forest","descriptions":["A series of narrow, twisty tracks wind their way through the forest in a somewhat aimless fashion.  All around you are trees and bushes, bushes and trees, and they all seem to look pretty much the same."],"exits":[{"to":137,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":98,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":137,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":137,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":101,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":137,"x":20,"y":-380,"z":0,"title":"Riverhaven Wilds, Forest","descriptions":["The twists and turns of the winding tracks get rather confusing.  With the sky hidden from view overhead, and no readily discernable difference in the trees around you, it is nearly impossible to determine the right track to follow to escape this maze of trees."],"exits":[{"to":136,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":137,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":136,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":137,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":137,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":138,"x":60,"y":-500,"z":0,"title":"West Wilds, Oak Room","descriptions":["This small circular room seems to have been carved from the living heart of the great oak.  A slender red candle rests atop a small bookcase and burns with a seemingly ceaseless flame, casting a steady glowing reflection on the highly polished walls around it.  The floor of the room is adorned with woven wool carpets, the once rich colors now somewhat faded with age, but the texture still soft and thick to the touch."],"exits":[{"to":107,"exit":"go","move":"touch candle;go portal"}]},
  {"id":139,"x":220,"y":-480,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest","descriptions":["Bark curls in pale strips from the trunks of birch trees.  Wide-leafed hosta grow in a circle around their base, thriving in the dim light of the forest.  The undergrowth is thinner, with fewer thorns, and you can hear the rush of water nearby."],"exits":[{"to":184,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":140,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":140,"x":220,"y":-460,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest","descriptions":["Feathery ferns crowned with thick, cinnamon-red spikes nestle in the shade of the trees.  The trail winds around in the lazy meandering pattern typical of deer paths everywhere.  To the north, the faint burble of running water can be heard through the brush."],"exits":[{"to":139,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":141,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":142,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":141,"x":260,"y":-460,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest","descriptions":["Leathery dark green leaves flutter on bushes that grow beneath the trees, twisting to reveal a thick-veined bronze underside.  Birds swoop amongst the branches, carrying bits and pieces of grass and vines to mend their nests."],"exits":[{"to":142,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":140,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":142,"x":240,"y":-440,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest","descriptions":["As the trees grow further apart, the path becomes more narrow.  Thick mounds of brush crowd the trail, competing for the sunlight and catching at passersby.  Clumps of fur caught in the grasping branches hint at others who haunt the forest.  Since the fur is about waist-high on a Gor'Tog, these others are perhaps more dangerous than an occasional thorn."],"exits":[{"to":141,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":143,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":146,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":140,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":143,"x":280,"y":-440,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest","descriptions":["Red-leafed vines twined around the trunks and lower branches of the trees lend a splash of vivid color to the dark greens and browns.  The leafless limbs of a dead tree let in dim light to brush the forest floor, heightening the shadows.","Red-leafed vines twined around the trunks and lower branches of the trees lend a splash of vivid color to the dark greens and browns.  The leafless limbs of a dead tree let in light to brush the forest floor, heightening the dim shadows."],"exits":[{"to":144,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":145,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":142,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":144,"x":280,"y":-420,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest","descriptions":["Still and somber, pine trees lower their branches to brush the ground, drooping like dejected suitors mourning their lost loves.  The melancholy limbs show a distressing tendency to clutch at travelers trying to make their way through the forest, jabbing sharp needles into exposed skin."],"exits":[{"to":143,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":145,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":145,"x":260,"y":-400,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest","descriptions":["Blight stalks the forest, leaving behind it a meandering track of dead trees, their bark peeled away in ragged curls to reveal weathered grey wood beneath.  Birds nest in the branches and hollows, and foxes or badgers lay claim to the burrows beneath the roots, but eventually the rotted wood will fall and join the decomposing leaves that carpet the forest floor."],"exits":[{"to":143,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":147,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":146,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":144,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":146,"x":240,"y":-400,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest","descriptions":["Birds chitter in the branches -- the warbling song of a wren, the shrill scolding of a scarlet jay, the hoarse call of a large crow -- all competing in a cacophonous clash of sound that masks the rustle of dead leaves as you move."],"exits":[{"to":142,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":145,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":147,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":148,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":147,"x":260,"y":-380,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest","descriptions":["High above, the trees' spreading branches are silhouetted against the star-lit sky.  On the forest floor, the land is cloaked in a perpetual green-tinged darkness broken from time to time by silvery shafts of moonlight piercing the canopy overhead.  Leaves crackle underfoot, a dried carpet over the thick, rich mulch.","High above, the trees vie with one another in their bloodless battle for the light.  On the forest floor, the land is cloaked in a perpetual green-tinged twilight broken from time to time by gilded shafts of sunlight piercing the canopy overhead.  Leaves crackle underfoot, a dried carpet over the thick, rich mulch."],"exits":[{"to":145,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":146,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":148,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":148,"x":240,"y":-340,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest","descriptions":["Clusters of river birch grow in pale grey stands along the edge of the clearing.  Beyond, the forest looms, tall and dark.  Mossy green vines dangle from overhanging limbs, modestly concealing the tree's trunk from view and masking the approach of anything that might be moving within the woods.  It's impossible to see which way to go to find the path in the forest."],"exits":[{"to":0,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":0,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":0,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":0,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":150,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":0,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":0,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":0,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":149,"exit":"climb","move":"objsearch rocky.ledge climb shrub"}]},
  {"id":149,"x":220,"y":-380,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Rocky Outcropping","descriptions":["The rock face angles outward above the ledge, making it impossible to climb past this point.  Below, you can see the deer paths' meandering track through the forest, twisting and turning in a logic known only to the deer."],"exits":[{"to":148,"exit":"down","move":"down"},{"to":146,"exit":"none","move":"script mistwoodcliff"}]},
  {"id":150,"x":240,"y":-300,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest","descriptions":["At the top of a rocky outcropping, you can look down onto a thicket of menacing briars.  No way down is readily apparent, and the thought of dropping thrice the height of a Gor'Tog into the thorns is really not something a sane person would wish to entertain."],"exits":[{"to":148,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":151,"exit":"climb","move":"objsearch outcropping climb handholds"}]},
  {"id":151,"x":240,"y":-280,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest","descriptions":["Narrow cracks in the rock wall provide precarious hand- and footholds as you climb.  Sharp-leafed shrubs cling tenaciously to the surface, their roots threading fragile tendrils into almost invisible cracks in their search for water."],"exits":[{"to":150,"exit":"climb","move":"climb wall"},{"to":152,"exit":"climb","move":"climb handholds"}]},
  {"id":152,"x":240,"y":-260,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest","descriptions":["A rocky outcropping juts up from the forest floor, surrounded by a tangle of briars along the base.  The trail ends here.  Bristly shrubs cling to the almost vertical surface in a triumph of faith over gravity, but appear too fragile to bear the weight of even the lightest Gnome."],"exits":[{"to":153,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":151,"exit":"climb","move":"objsearch outcrop climb handholds"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":153,"x":220,"y":-240,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest","descriptions":["The path winds back and forth between tall, thin conifers that tower toward the sky, allowing only dappled patches of moonlight to filter through to the forest floor.  An occasional thick-trunked oak or graceful stands of birch compete for light and nutrients with the faster-growing pines.","The path winds back and forth between tall, thin conifers that tower toward the sky, allowing only dappled patches of sunlight to filter through to the forest floor.  An occasional thick-trunked oak or graceful stands of birch compete for light and nutrients with the faster-growing pines."],"exits":[{"to":152,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":154,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":154,"x":240,"y":-220,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest","descriptions":["Fallen logs, bark peeled away to reveal weathered grey wood beneath, are arranged in a semicircle around a rock-lined fire pit.  The ashes are cold now, but wood piled between two saplings marks this as a frequent resting place for travelers."],"exits":[{"to":155,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":153,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#008000","aliases":["RTT14","RT-MFG-HWG"]},
  {"id":155,"x":240,"y":-200,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["A dog barks outside an isolated cabin, its shrill \"yip, yip, yip\" breaking the silence of the surrounding forest.  To the south, the darkness of the fir trees give way to open farmland and low, rolling hills.","A dog barks outside an isolated cabin, its shrill yip, yip, yip breaking the silence of the surrounding forest.  To the south, the darkness of the fir trees give way to open farmland and low, rolling hills."],"exits":[{"to":154,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":156,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":156,"x":220,"y":-180,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["The trail rises, cresting atop a small hill.  To the north, the far side of the valley is covered in trees that sway ponderously in the wind, waving back and forth in a slow and stately dance silhouetted against the night sky.","The trail rises, cresting atop a small hill.  To the north, the far side of the valley is covered in trees that sway ponderously in the wind, waving back and forth in a slow and stately green dance.  Dark green oaks, paler maples, the near-black needles on the conical pines and the quaking limbs of aspens with their flashes of silver as the wind tosses their leaves -- the forest is host to a subtle parade of colors."],"exits":[{"to":155,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":157,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":157,"x":220,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["The ground grows dark as rich pasture land gives way to rocky slopes.  Water burbles through a crack in the rocks, trickling slowly into a small pool.  Cattails and iris grow in cheerful profusion along the shore, and an occasional bullfrog splashes, unseen, but not unheard."],"exits":[{"to":156,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":158,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":158,"x":240,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["Huddled mounds of cream-colored fleece, barely visible in the nearby fields, mark the presence of a sheep farm.  Tufts of wool sway from low branches, and in the distance, the soft glow of a fire wards off the predators in the darkness.","Cream-colored sheep graze in the grass, oblivious to those passing along the lane.  Heads down, they focus solely on the transfer of greenery from ground to stomach."],"exits":[{"to":159,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":157,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":159,"x":260,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["A wooden stile leads over a fence, allowing travelers to continue along the curving road or chance a short cut across the fields.  Faint ripples in the tall grass hint at the presence of some grazing animal, or a predator in stalk of its prey."],"exits":[{"to":160,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":158,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":172,"exit":"go","move":"go wooden stile"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":160,"x":240,"y":-120,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["Wind whistles through sandstone menhirs, some still standing in defiance of the elements, others sprawled gracelessly upon the grassy verge.  White stains on the rocks bear mute witness to the presence of local birds."],"exits":[{"to":159,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":161,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":161,"x":240,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["The land beside the trail grows steeper to the south as the road passes through a series of rolling hills.  The scholars who study the movement of the earth call these types of hills drumlins, with long explanations of how the air and water elementals work together to form glaciers which cool the earth heated by the World Dragon's presence.  When the glaciers recede, the dragon's shivering forms the low rolling hills."],"exits":[{"to":160,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":162,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":162,"x":260,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["The slopes beside the trail grow increasingly rocky, though low shrubs cling with tenacious determination to their footholds.  Clusters of vivid blue flowers dot the greenery just out of reach from the path."],"exits":[{"to":163,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":161,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":163,"x":240,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["Low hills, about twice the height of a Gor'Tog, rise along either side of the path in green-robed splendor.  The mounds offer shelter from the winds and a home to badgers and cliff swallows."],"exits":[{"to":162,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":164,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":164,"x":240,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["The trail narrows to a packed dirt path, barely wide enough for a single cart.  Wooden wheels have left deep ruts in which water gathers after the rain.  To judge by the thick carpet of grass growing along the side of the ruts, wagons are few and far between."],"exits":[{"to":163,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":165,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":165,"x":220,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["A low mound rises in the middle of a nearby pasture, shaded by the spreading limbs of a pin oak tree.  The grass is tall and green, fed by a gentle brook that runs through a clay culvert beneath the road.  Sheep meander through the greenery, cropping at the grain and baaing plaintively."],"exits":[{"to":164,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":166,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":169,"exit":"go","move":"go pasture"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":166,"x":240,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["The passage of wagons traveling from local farms to the town of Riverhaven has left rutted, mud-filled tracks in the dirt trail.  A granite marker stands beside the road."],"exits":[{"to":167,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":165,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":167,"x":240,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["The road twists and turns as it passes through hedgerows that separate it from the fields.  Beyond, sheep dot the hillside as they graze on golden hay almost ready to be cut.  Bits of wool adorn the hedge here and there, soft cream against the dark green leaves."],"exits":[{"to":166,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":168,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":168,"x":240,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["Faded red bricks, once neatly laid in a herringbone pattern, now exist only as scraps of pavement heaved up and broken by years of neglect.  Weeds grow through the crumbled mortar, obscuring the direction of the road.  Wild roses climb in a high thicket along the northern side of the road to form a tangled mass of sweetly scented thorns."],"exits":[{"to":167,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":27,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#008000","aliases":["RTT13","RT-HWG-MFG"]},
  {"id":169,"x":170,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Ceceline's Meadow, Along the Road","descriptions":["The grass has grown up around the fence as if determined to reclaim the road on the far side.  Though the tracks left by years of passing wagons are still somewhat visible, nature makes an ongoing effort to recover the land stolen from it."],"exits":[{"to":170,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":165,"exit":"go","move":"go road"}]},
  {"id":170,"x":150,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Ceceline's Meadow, Along the Road","descriptions":["A small hole in the side of a grassy slope is almost entirely concealed by the lush plants growing around it.  Near the entrance is a mound of earth, indicating that the digging was done recently.  In various places nearby, the grass has been cropped by the local sheep."],"exits":[{"to":171,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":169,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":180,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"aliases":["Barghest"]},
  {"id":171,"x":150,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Ceceline's Meadow, Along the Road","descriptions":["A large rock juts out of the surrounding grass, its weathered and grey surface visible in spite of the best efforts of the surrounding vegetation.  On its south side, a rusty red discoloration mars the surface of the stone."],"exits":[{"to":172,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":170,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":174,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":173,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":172,"x":170,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Ceceline's Meadow, Along the Road","descriptions":["Tall grass grows up around the stile that separates this meadow from the more traveled road.  The plants are so insistent on not giving up the least bit of space that they've crowded in around the fence posts, hiding the lower part of the stile entirely from view."],"exits":[{"to":171,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":173,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":159,"exit":"go","move":"go wooden stile"}]},
  {"id":173,"x":130,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Ceceline's Meadow","descriptions":["Each gentle breeze invites the tall grasses to dance and leaves them swaying gracefully to an unheard song.  The fence at this part of the meadow appears to have suffered some trauma -- a long cracked dent runs through one of the posts as if something has crashed into it with a great deal of force."],"exits":[{"to":172,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":171,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":174,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":178,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":175,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":174,"x":130,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Ceceline's Meadow","descriptions":["A looming pillar of darkness blocks out much of the sky to the west, though a few moments of careful observation resolve the shape into that of a large tree.  The tall grasses, now cloaked by shadow, give the ground a false appearance of being uneven and treacherous.","Directly to the west, a pin oak tree rises proudly from the carpet of grass, making all smaller plants look miniature by comparison.  A scattering of tiny acorns has escaped the looming shadow of its parent but they have yet to make their way into the ground and begin to challenge the great oak's supremacy."],"exits":[{"to":173,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":171,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":180,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":178,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":175,"x":110,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Ceceline's Meadow","descriptions":["The land curves up on all sides, leaving a shallow hollow in the ground.  The small bush that has taken up residence at its bottom grows lush and dark, perhaps benefiting from extra servings of water carried down these mild slopes each time it rains."],"exits":[{"to":173,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":178,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":176,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":176,"x":100,"y":-91,"z":0,"title":"Ceceline's Meadow","descriptions":["The grasses in this particular area have been cropped closer to the ground, though there's no sign of why the local wildlife would have a preference for this spot.  In spite of their persecution, the plants valiantly continue to stretch skyward."],"exits":[{"to":175,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":178,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":177,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":177,"x":100,"y":-70,"z":0,"title":"Ceceline's Meadow","descriptions":["In the quiet of the night, plants lean in against each other, all rivalries cast aside as they conserve strength for the coming day's struggle for sunlight.  The grasses closest to the fence take advantage of its strength, resting close to its lowest rung as if in fatigue.","The vibrance and density of the local plants steadily increase at a distance from the deep shadows cast by the pin oak growing just to the northeast.  Branches as thick as a Gor'Tog's arm stretch out from the tree, but even such a mighty specimen cannot shade all the world, in spite of its best efforts."],"exits":[{"to":176,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":178,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":179,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":178,"x":110,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Ceceline's Meadow, Beneath the Oak","descriptions":["A variety of miniature acorns lies scattered across the ground, variations in the amount of damage they've accrued hinting at the variety of years represented.  The great oak stretches its branches down toward the ground as if to protect its offspring, seemingly oblivious to the suffocating nature of the shade it provides."],"exits":[{"to":175,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":173,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":174,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":180,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":179,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":177,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":176,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":181,"exit":"climb","move":"climb oak"}]},
  {"id":179,"x":110,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Ceceline's Meadow","descriptions":["Cheery blue flowers luxuriate in the shelter provided by a flat grey rock leaned against its brother at an angle.  Though the blooms peek out into the open in hopes of attracting wandering insects to their vibrant petals, the space through which they reach is sufficiently narrow to protect them from the hungry teeth of grazing animals."],"exits":[{"to":178,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":180,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":177,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":180,"x":130,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Ceceline's Meadow","descriptions":["There are several deep notches in the fence, so cleanly cut that they must have been made by a well-honed weapon, though why someone would have attacked an inanimate object is unclear.  To the west, a flowering plant is visible, the vivid blue of its flowers easily drawing attention among the surrounding greens and greys."],"exits":[{"to":174,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":170,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":179,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":178,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":181,"x":80,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Pin Oak, Lower Branches","descriptions":["The lowest branches in the tree are thick and strong, tilting down toward the ground in an invitation to greater feats of climbing.  In the side of the trunk itself, some young lover has carved his beloved's initials, framed by a crude heart."],"exits":[{"to":178,"exit":"climb","move":"climb trunk"},{"to":182,"exit":"climb","move":"climb middle branches"}]},
  {"id":182,"x":80,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Pin Oak, Midway","descriptions":["Midway up the trunk, the branches stretch out almost perfectly parallel to the ground.  The bases of the branches are largely free of leaves and offshoots, such that a spot where several burly branches have grown in close proximity makes for a secure perch, even in the darkness.  Farther out on the limbs, leaves grow thickly enough to block out any stars that might otherwise have been visible, closing around in such a way as to give the impression of being sealed in a cocoon.","Midway up the trunk, branches stretch out almost perfectly parallel to the ground.  Their bases are largely free of leaves and offshoots, and a spot where several burly branches have grown in close proximity makes for a rather comfortable seat.  Farther out on the limbs, leaves grow thick and vibrant, making this spot the center of a secure cocoon of greenery."],"exits":[{"to":181,"exit":"climb","move":"climb lower branches"},{"to":183,"exit":"climb","move":"climb upper branches"}]},
  {"id":183,"x":80,"y":-120,"z":0,"title":"Pin Oak, Treetop","descriptions":["At the very top of the tree, the branches grow more ambitious and stretch out toward the sky.  From this height the ground is almost impossible to see, though the lights of a city are just barely discernable to the south.","The branches here grow thinner and more impatient for light.  They strain upward, intent on gathering every stray bit of precious energy that the sun sees fit to bestow, leaving little more than a pool of shadow for the grasses growing far below."],"exits":[{"to":182,"exit":"climb","move":"climb middle branches"}]},
  {"id":184,"x":240,"y":-500,"z":0,"title":"Jantspyre River, South Bank","descriptions":["The forest gives way to the banks of a swift-flowing river.  No bridge crosses the water, and the far bank is too steep to clamber out."],"exits":[{"to":139,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":185,"exit":"go","move":"go bank"}]},
  {"id":185,"x":240,"y":-520,"z":0,"title":"Jantspyre River, In the Water","descriptions":["Crystal clear water tumbles, icy cold, over the rounded pebbles of the streambed.  Spray slicks the dark grey rocks on either side.  The current pushes you toward the south bank where, despite the wet surface, an agile climber could probably scramble out of the water.  Just downstream, the creek flows over a pile of logs tumbled higgledy-piggledy like some giant's jackstraws."],"exits":[{"to":0,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":184,"exit":"go","move":"go bank"}],"aliases":["Mistwood Forest","Rossman's Landing","Therenborough","Langenfirth"],"linksTo":"Map34_Mistwood_Forest.xml"}
 ],
 "labels": [
